language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ five_statements: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Determine which of the following statements is true.
$ - Exactly one of these statements is false.
$ - Exactly two of these statements are false.
$ - Exactly three of these statements are false.
$ - Exactly four of these statements are false.
$ - Exactly five of these statements are false.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/five_statements.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ the number of statements
letting n = 5
$ statements[k]: statement k (k = 1..5, in the order listed) is true
find statements : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool

such that
$ statement k is true exactly when exactly k of the five statements are false
forAll k : int(1..n) . (statements[k] <-> ((sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(statements[i] = false)) = k))
